## 1. Introduction

JFK Airport is one of the busiest international airports in the United States, serving over 60 million passengers annually. Given the scale of operations, effective ground handling and security processes are crucial to ensuring passenger safety and operational efficiency. This report presents a detailed analysis of the terminal operations at JFK, focusing on the following key areas:

1. Ground Operations
2. Airline Collaborations
3. Security Protocols
4. Technology Integration

